// std::retaining: DIN 471 (shaft) and DIN 472 (bore) retaining rings and grooves (stdlib.md 1, 2).
//
// Keyed by the nominal shaft (Din471) or bore (Din472) diameter d1 in mm.
// Columns: groove_dia (d2), groove_width (m), ring_thickness (s) and
// edge_margin (n, the minimum groove edge to the shaft end or housing face).
// groove_dia and groove_width carry the tolerance class DIN prints for the
// groove (h10/H13 shaft, H11/H13 bore); ring_thickness is the nominal s and its
// deviation is written on the ots that uses it (golden 02). edge_margin is a
// minimum and is untoleranced.
//
// PROVENANCE WARNING: figures were entered from recall of the DIN tables,
// not transcribed from the standards; the std citation audit must verify
// every row against DIN 471:2022 and DIN 472:2022 before release.
// Sizes listed are the preferred sizes 3..75 (Din471) and 8..75 (Din472) mm.

/// The citation for the shaft-ring table: DIN 471.
pub cite din471: standard {
    organization = "DIN"
    number = "DIN 471"
    title = "Retaining rings for shafts, normal type"
    date = "2022"
    note = "Groove dimensions"
}

/// The citation for the bore-ring table: DIN 472.
pub cite din472: standard {
    organization = "DIN"
    number = "DIN 472"
    title = "Retaining rings for bores, normal type"
    date = "2022"
    note = "Groove dimensions"
}

